 Image drvfuzz:local Built 
Builds an implementation-specific program from the testcase_config (optionally overriding the ISA base) and writes testcase.json, user_instructions.asm, program.S, and ELF outputs under --run-dir. With --minimal-artifacts only the assembly and ELF are emitted.

Usage: DRVFuzz generate [OPTIONS] --config <TESTCASE_CONFIG> --riscv-impl <RISCV_IMPL> --run-dir <RUN_DIR>

Options:
      --config <TESTCASE_CONFIG>
          TOML file containing the [testcase_config] used to generate instructions

      --riscv-impl <RISCV_IMPL>
          Target implementation; initialization and extensions are tailored to this core
          
          [possible values: spike, rocket, boom-v3, boom-v4, pico-rv32, cva6, xiang-shan, ibex, vex, kronos, srv32]

      --isa <ISA>
          Optional override for the isa_base in the config (rv32 or rv64)
          
          [possible values: rv32, rv64]

      --run-dir <RUN_DIR>
          Directory that will store generated instructions and ELF outputs

      --minimal-artifacts
          Emit only program.S/.s and ELF artifacts; skip testcase.json and instruction snapshot

      --sdmodel
          Enable the SDModel sensitive-data generator for boundary values and exception triggers

      --sdmodel-probability <SDMODEL_PROBABILITY>
          Override SDModel injection probability (0.0 to 1.0)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
